A microservices architecture diagram. Style: architecture.

Services and connections:
- Client (browser/mobile) sends requests to an API Gateway
- API Gateway routes to three backend services: User Service, Order Service, and Product Service
- User Service reads/writes from a Users Database (PostgreSQL)
- Order Service reads/writes from an Orders Database (PostgreSQL) and publishes events to a Message Queue (RabbitMQ)
- Product Service reads/writes from a Products Database (MongoDB)
- A Notification Service subscribes to the Message Queue and sends emails/push notifications
- All services emit logs to a centralized Logging Service
